Implement Qwen Image 2.1 base model import

Upstream ships Qwen Image 2.1 inference and LoRA import but converts the
base model out of tree. The importer arms are lifted from LoRAImporter's
working .qwenImage2_1 wiring.

Comfy-Org's repackage fuses the SwiGLU halves as img_mlp.gate_up, gate
rows first, so the block mappers now accept that name as well.

txt_in.text_norm is zero-centred, and the catalog's converted ckpt stores
1 + raw. The importer applies the shift itself because LoRAImporter writes
a LoRA's .diff through the model's own mapper, where a shift would add 1
to a norm delta.

Base and Turbo share one tensor set and differ only in base's
shift_terminal, so the schedule is chosen by the file name. The quantizer
keeps context_norm raw, as the catalog's q6p does.
